                <pb facs="0703" n="595" sameAs="frus:frus1927v02/pg595"/>

                <note rend="inline" type="source">123 So 8/140: Telegram</note>
                <head><hi rendition="#italic">The Vice Consul at Aden</hi> (<hi rendition="#italic"
                        >Park</hi>) <hi rendition="#italic">to the Secretary of State</hi></head>
                <opener><dateline rendition="#float-right"><placeName><hi rendition="#small-caps"
                                >Aden</hi></placeName>, <date calendar="gregorian"
                            when="1927-10-24T23:00:00+03:00"><hi rendition="#italic">October 24,
                                1927—11 p.m.</hi></date><lb/>[Received October 25—2:39
                        a.m.]</dateline></opener>
                <p>Referring to Department’s telegram of October 17, 8 p.m. I have just received a
                    telegraphic communication from Ras Tafari stating that he is greatly pleased
                    that Mr. Southard whom he counts as a personal friend of long standing has been
                    selected to establish the new Legation at Addis Ababa,</p>
                <closer><signed><hi rendition="#small-caps">Park</hi></signed></closer>
            </div>
        </body>
